nna do invite you to write you know  chapter in their book but what really  really matters is whether you can  explain Aristotle to somebody who really  hasn't had much background in philosophy  and show them why Aristotle's  Nicomachean ethics could transform their  life their career their relationships  reorient them to what it is that they're  doing in the world because that text can  do that or take Epictetus discourses or  take you know  I mean I've gone so far as to teach  Hegel in intro to philosophy classes  people say that's crazy how could those  students possibly be up to it well you  know these students will surprise you if  you actually put in the work yourself to  do it so I think that that we should  make this a mandatory part of you know  teaching for everybody across the board  I I'm sure you could get other people  behind it it would be very unpopular  among the professor it but it would be  so wonderful and there would be so many  of them who after a while would say oh I  get it I understand  I see why that was important some of  them would be kicking and screaming the  entire time all the way up till  retirement but others would also say no  there was a point to this exercise I can  say that myself is the last thing I'll  say from 20 years of putting in work  doing service classes or preparing to  you know other people to teach service  classes because I also coach other  professors I think it's really valuable  I think that you know we should be  reaching as wide an audience as possible  people accuse us of popularizing or  watering things down you don't have to  water anything down you can teach  ordinary people great philosophy but you  have to really work your butt off as an  instructor to do that and I think that  there's a lot of people who haven't put  in the time they could put in the time  I'm not saying they don't have the  talent they don't have the capacity to  do it but they haven't put in the time  to do that and so they write it off I  think we need to have a you know  transvaluation of our perspectives in  this sort of case so that's what I'm  going to close on that's my rant about  this time  [Music]

